---
// Mount point for lesson 13's side-by-side board. The intro is server-rendered so
// the lesson still says something without JavaScript, and so the opening copy
// lives in one place. Everything after the button is built at runtime by
// src/scripts/courses/sameevent/sameevent.ts.
//
// It runs after the prose has shown both objects, because the board is somewhere
// to watch the difference rather than somewhere to learn the fields.
import "@styles/sameevent.css";
---

<div data-sameevent>
  <div class="se not-prose my-8">
    <div data-se-stage>
      <div class="se-shell">
        <div class="se-intro">
          <p>
            Three nodes running a Deployment, a DaemonSet and a StatefulSet side by
            side. Do something to the cluster and see what each of them does about
            it.
          </p>
          <div class="se-foot">
            <button type="button" class="se-btn" data-tone="primary" data-go="start"
              >Open the cluster</button
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <noscript>
      <p class="se-note mt-3">
        This board needs JavaScript. The short version: delete a pod and the
        Deployment makes one with a new name anywhere, the DaemonSet makes one on
        the same node, and the StatefulSet brings back the same name with the same
        disk. Add a node and only the DaemonSet reacts. Cut a node off and the
        Deployment replaces its pod within minutes, while the StatefulSet waits,
        because it won't risk two pods with one name.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  import "@scripts/courses/sameevent/sameevent";
</script>
